      "target": "sql_viewer",
      "params": {},
      "narration": "Here's our database. We've got two tables. The orders table has order ID, region, order date, gross revenue, subtotal, discount amount, refund amount, is test order, and status. Then there's a shipments table with shipment ID, order ID, shipped date, and carrier. Pretty standard e-commerce setup. The trouble starts when these two tables meet in a JOIN.",
