    {
      "id": "e27",
      "time_offset_ms": 415649,
      "type": "show_result",
      "target": "sql_viewer",
      "params": {},
      "narration": "Interesting. 12 total rows, total discount with COALESCE is 30,756.25, total discount without COALESCE is also 30,756.25, and the difference is 0.00. In this case, adding COALESCE didn't change the sum because the NULL rows had no numeric value to add. But here's the point, you didn't know that until you checked. And with AVG it would've mattered, because AVG divides by the count of non-NULL values. Fewer values in the denominator means a higher average. Always check, always decide explicitly.",
