      "narration": "Look at this. Order 1001, UTC timestamp January 1st at 3:14 AM. Convert that to Eastern and it's December 31st at 10:14 PM. The UTC date says January 1st, but Eastern says December 31st. Gross revenue, 42,750.00. That order lives in January if you're in UTC, but December if you're in Eastern. Same story with order 1014, UTC January 1st at 2:30 AM becomes December 31st at 9:30 PM Eastern, with 38,740.00 in revenue. And then there's order 1015, UTC February 1st at 4:15 AM, which becomes January 31st at 11:15 PM Eastern, 27,580.00. That one shifts into January when you switch to Eastern. Order 1008 also shifts, UTC January 18th at 1:10 AM becomes January 17th at 8:10 PM Eastern, gross revenue 14,760.00.",
